---
title: Placing the start
---
Decide where the start should be, then put it on the nearest tile that is open [[t:241-243 s:25]].

## The rule
1. Choose a desired point:
   - `left`: the middle of the left edge [[c17:70]];
   - `center`: the center of the map [[c19:69]].
2. The start goes on the open tile nearest that point, in a straight line [[c17:69-86]].

- **On a culled map:** the demo culls first, so the start can walk to everything that is left [[c17:34-67 t:236-237]].
- **Talk says:** place somewhere in the middle on the left, then look around for a neighboring tile that is open and hasn’t been culled [[t:241-243]].

